# Git commits - hard rules

## Stop conditions

- Do **not** `git commit` unless the user explicitly asks to commit.
- Do **not** `git push` unless the user explicitly asks to push.
- Do **not** use `--no-verify` / `--no-gpg-sign` unless the user explicitly asks.

## Authors

Only these humans:

- `dinesh-ad <56721895+dinesh-ad@users.noreply.github.com>`
- `sowmipriya <13678035+sowmipriya@users.noreply.github.com>`

## Forbidden in commit messages (strict)

Never add any of these to the subject, body, or trailers:

- `Co-authored-by:` for Claude, Anthropic, Cursor, Copilot, OpenAI, ChatGPT, Codex, Gemini, Devin, Windsurf, Aider, Codeium, Tabnine, Perplexity, or any other AI/tool
- Emails such as `noreply@anthropic.com`, `cursoragent@…`, `@cursor.com` / `.so` / `.sh`, `@openai.com`, and similar tool domains
- `Generated with Claude|Cursor|Copilot|…`, `Made with Cursor|…`, robot attribution lines
- Unicode em dash (U+2014) in the commit message (use ASCII `-`)

If a tool injected a forbidden line, **remove it immediately** before the commit is created. Hooks in `.githooks/` strip (`prepare-commit-msg`) and reject (`commit-msg` / `pre-commit`).

Allowed `Co-authored-by` **only** for the two humans above (exact emails).

